 \\(H_{i}\\).  Hence all non\u2011diagonal cells are covered,\n   and each row and each column contains exactly one uncovered cell\u2014the\n   diagonal one.\n\n   Thus the lower bound \\(2n-2\\) is attainable.\n\n4. **Application to the original board** \u2013  \n   For the given \\(2025\\times2025\\) grid we have \\(n=2025\\).  Substituting in\n   the formula gives  \n\n   \\[\n   \\text{minimum number of tiles}=2\\cdot2025-2=4048 .\n   \\]\n\n   The explicit tiling described above (vertical tiles below the main diagonal\n   and horizontal tiles to the right of the diagonal) uses exactly 4048\n   tiles and satisfies all the required conditions.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{4048}\n\\]"
